---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
const carris = [
  { t: 'Sintra and Cabo da Roca', x: 'Line 1624, Cascais (Terminal) to Portela de Sintra (Estação Norte, the north train station) via Cabo da Roca. VERIFIED that the line exists (Carris Metropolitana open data, re-checked 25 Nov 2026). Its timetable was not checked. Line 1253, Sintra (Estação) via Cabo da Roca, is a loop that starts in Sintra. VERIFIED (same data).' },
  { t: 'Sintra (other)', x: 'Lines 1620, 1621 and 1623 run from Cascais (Terminal) to Portela de Sintra (Estação Sul, the south train station). 1621 goes via CascaiShopping (Terminal). VERIFIED that they exist (same data, re-checked 25 Nov 2026).' },
  { t: 'Sintra: "Estação Sul" or "Estação Norte"?', x: 'Per the line names, 1620, 1621 and 1623 end at Portela de Sintra (Estação Sul, south station), and 1624 (the Cabo da Roca line) ends at Portela de Sintra (Estação Norte, north station). No official page was found that says what each stop is for or how it connects to Sintra town, so why to choose one is NOT CONFIRMED. The stop data does show Portela de Sintra has "Entrada Norte" and "Entrada Sul" platforms (VERIFIED), with 1624 using the north entrance and 1620, 1621, 1623, 1626, 1629 and 1630 the south. Check the stop on the Carris Metropolitana app before you go. See Getting around Sintra below for what happens once you arrive.' },
  { t: 'The mall (CascaiShopping)', x: 'Line 1621 above runs via CascaiShopping, and 1626 runs CascaiShopping (Terminal) to Portela de Sintra. VERIFIED that they exist. These are longer lines, so for a local trip to the mall use MobiCascais.' },
  { t: 'Hospital de Cascais (Dr. José de Almeida)', x: 'There is a Carris Metropolitana stop named "Hospital de Cascais" (Alcabideche, stop 050233). VERIFIED from the Carris Metropolitana stop data (re-checked 25 Nov 2026). Lines listed for it: 1620, 1623, 1625, 1626, 1627, 1628, 1629, 1630, 1631 and 1639. By their line names, 1620, 1623, 1625 and 1639 start at Cascais Terminal, 1626 and 1627 at CascaiShopping, and 1628 to 1631 at Estoril station. Lines 1621 and 1624 are not listed for this stop.' },
  { t: 'CUF Cascais (Hospital CUF Cascais, Rua Fernão Lopes 60)', x: 'The closest Carris Metropolitana stops are on Av. Eng. Adelino Amaro da Costa, "Av Eng Adelino Amaro Costa 1156" (050259) and "1141" (050260), about 150 m in a straight line from the hospital\'s map point on cuf.pt. Only line 1624 (Cascais to Sintra via Cabo da Roca) is listed for them. VERIFIED from the Carris Metropolitana stop data. The distance is calculated from the stop coordinates and the map point on cuf.pt, so treat it as approximate (PROBABLY TRUE).' },
];
const mobi = [
  { t: 'Guincho (the beach)', x: 'M05 (via Quinta da Marinha), M15 (via Areia) and M43 run from Cascais train station as loops (circular) and are listed as going via or to Guincho. VERIFIED from the MobiCascais line list as read on an earlier date (not re-checked 25 Nov 2026; MobiCascais site not reachable for re-check). Stop lists were not read.' },
  { t: 'Hospital de Cascais (Dr. José de Almeida)', x: 'There is a bus stop named "Hospital de Cascais" (MobiCascais stop 20005). OpenStreetMap volunteer tags list M01, M03, M10, M17, M20, M22, M28 and M31 on one platform and M39 and M40 on another. PROBABLY TRUE (not re-checked 25 Nov 2026): third-party tags, but M17, M31 and M40 match MobiCascais\'s own line names, and M17 (Cascais Terminal to Bairro da Cadeia do Linhó via Alvide and the hospital) is the one that starts at Cascais Terminal. Check the others in the MobiCascais app.' },
  { t: 'The mall (CascaiShopping)', x: 'M03 (loop via Torre), M29 (from São João do Estoril station), M38 (from Estoril station) and M01 (from Parede) are listed as serving it. PROBABLY TRUE (not re-checked 25 Nov 2026). A numbered line straight from Cascais Terminal was not confirmed.' },
  { t: 'Estoril and the casino', x: 'M06, M07, M11, M12 and M13 run between Cascais Terminal and Estoril train station. VERIFIED for the line list (earlier read, not re-checked 25 Nov 2026). The stop nearest the Casino Estoril is NOT CONFIRMED.' },
  { t: 'CUF Cascais (Hospital CUF Cascais, Rua Fernão Lopes 60)', x: 'Closest stop found: "Rua Eça de Queiroz" (MobiCascais stop 20895), about 85 m in a straight line from the hospital\'s map point, tagged for M09 and M22. A second stop on Av. Eng. Adelino Amaro da Costa, "Colégio Quadrante" (stop 20886, about 150 m), is tagged M02 and M14. REASONABLY TRUE-UNVERIFIED (not re-checked 25 Nov 2026): OpenStreetMap volunteer tags, not an official page, and the map point comes from the link on cuf.pt. Check in the MobiCascais app.' },
];
---
<section id="cascais-buses" class="visit buses" aria-label="Buses from Cascais Terminal">
  <h2>Buses from Cascais Terminal</h2>
  <p class="muted"><strong>Carris Metropolitana and MobiCascais are two separate bus networks</strong> with their own line numbers, timetables and apps. MobiCascais is the Cascais council's system. Whether a ticket or card from one works on the other is NOT CONFIRMED, so check before you rely on it. People who live, study or work in Cascais ride the municipal MobiCascais lines free with a Viver Cascais card (VERIFIED: Cascais council data page, read 25 Nov 2026, undated). Hospital de Cascais (Dr. José de Almeida), CascaiShopping and CUF Cascais are used as example destinations. Line numbers change, so check the apps.</p>
  <div class="bus-cols">
    <div class="bus-col">
      <h3><span class="ic"><Icon name="bus" /></span>Carris Metropolitana</h3>
      {carris.map(r => <div class="bus-row"><h4>{r.t}</h4><p>{r.x}</p></div>)}
    </div>
    <div class="bus-col">
      <h3><span class="ic"><Icon name="bus" /></span>MobiCascais <small>(local Cascais system, M lines)</small></h3>
      {mobi.map(r => <div class="bus-row"><h4>{r.t}</h4><p>{r.x}</p></div>)}
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="bus-note"><strong>International schools:</strong> most run their own school buses. Carris Metropolitana stops in Linhó are served by lines 1620, 1623, 1626, 1629 and 1630, not by 1621 or 1624: the closest stop to CAISL is "R António dos Reis (Colégio Americano)" (about 120 m) and the closest to TASIS is "Alam do Linhó (Beloura Shopping)" (about 70 m). See <a href="#cascais-schools">International schools nearby</a>.</p>
  <p class="totop"><a href="#top">↑ Back to top</a></p>
</section>
<style is:global>
  .buses { margin:1.4rem 0; }
  .buses h2 { font-size:1.15rem; margin:0 0 .2rem; }
  .buses > p { margin:0 0 .7rem; font-size:.92rem; line-height:1.5; }
  .bus-cols { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:.8rem; align-items:start; }
  .bus-col { background:var(--teal-soft); border-radius:20px; padding:.8rem .9rem; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:.5rem; }
  .bus-col h3 { display:flex; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.5rem; margin:0; font-size:1.02rem; color:var(--teal); }
  .bus-col h3 small { font-weight:600; font-size:.8rem; }
  .bus-col .ic { display:grid; place-items:center; flex:none; width:2rem; height:2rem; border-radius:50%; background:var(--surface); color:var(--teal); } .bus-col .ic .i { --s:1.1rem; }
  .bus-row { background:var(--surface); border-radius:14px; padding:.55rem .85rem; }
  .bus-row h4 { margin:0 0 .15rem; font-size:.95rem; color:var(--teal); }
  .bus-row p { margin:0; font-size:.9rem; line-height:1.5; }
  .bus-note { margin:.7rem 0 0; font-size:.9rem; line-height:1.5; }
  @media (max-width:700px){ .bus-cols { grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr); } }
</style>
